# vectorxform2d

- Label: Vector Transform 2D
- Category: Copernicus (`Cop`), Houdini 22.0.368
- Inputs: 0 to 2
- Parameters: 12 (exact, read from Houdini by hython)
- Used by the height graph: no

## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/vectorxform2d.html
- Summary (EN): Transforms the values of a UV layer or attribute in 2D space. Each value is treated as an XY location, transformed, and written back as the new values. Output: the transformed layer.
- Résumé (FR) : Transforme en 2D les valeurs XY d'une couche UV, sans déplacer les pixels.

- Inputs meaning: ["source: the UV layer or attribute whose pixel values define the XY locations", "mask (optional): per-pixel mask scaled by the Mask parameter"]

- Key parameters: ["Mask: how much of the new value is blended with the original (default 1 uses only the new value)", "Order: sequence in which translate, rotate and scale are applied", "Translate, Rotate (degrees about the pivot), Scale (non-uniform), Shear (XY), Uniform Scale", "Pivot: pivot point for rotations and scales, in the value's coordinates", "Invert Transformation: inverts the computed transform before it is applied"]

- Caveats: ["The node does not move pixels; each pixel operates in place"]

